.TH geectl-remote-cat 1  "geectl-remote-cat 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-cat \- Print a source file to standard output. Text only: the library reads the file as a UTF\-8 string, so a binary file fails the call with a server error ("response body is not valid UTF\-8") instead of printing bytes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote cat\fR [\fB\-\-rev\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a source file to standard output. Text only: the library reads the file as a UTF\-8 string, so a binary file fails the call with a server error ("response body is not valid UTF\-8") instead of printing bytes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rev\fR \fI<REV>\fR
Print the file as of this revision (default: latest): a revision number or a srcmd5
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package lives in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package the file lives in
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
The file to print
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
